Project Title: ERBriwan: Emergency Response Button for Everyone
The ERBriwan mobile application serves as the central platform for sending and receiving emergency alerts integrated with a one-button emergency device. It enables users to transmit real-time location data and emergency type information to nearby registered responders, who can view alerts and navigate using a map-based interface. The application supports both sender and responder roles, ensuring fast, accurate, and coordinated emergency response.


General Objective:
	To develop an emergency response system that enables users to quickly send emergency alerts with their location using a single-button device integrated with a mobile application for faster and more efficient emergency response.
Specific Objectives:
To develop a mobile application that supports sender and responder roles through secure user and device registration.
To develop an emergency classification mechanism where each number of button clicks corresponds to a specific type of emergency, and allows users to send emergency alerts based on multiple button clicks to reduce false alarms.
To design live location tracking for the sender that is automatically transmitted to registered responders.
To develop continuous location updates for responders to support coordination and navigation during emergencies.
To directly notify the nearest available responders, such as police patrols, barangay tanods, or emergency personnel, based on the user’s active location.

To design and develop a map-based interface that allows responders to view the sender’s exact location and enables the sender to view the location of nearby and active responders.
To design an emergency alert history module for monitoring and documentation purposes.

 PROPOSED SYSTEM FEATURES
User and Device Registration
Emergency Alert Activation and Classification
Real-Time Location Tracking

Map-Based Emergency Monitoring
Instant Notifications to Responders
Responder Coordination and Navigation
Emergency Alert History and Logs
User Accountability and Misuse Prevention


